 "rule": "Written before it was run (12 Oct). It picks the candidate's model and THETA for docs/SAME_DAY_YES_PREREG.md on dates already inspected, and says how they did there. These dates chose the values, so their result flatters the candidate; only the forward dates test it. THE DECISIONS: the walk-forward dump with the remaining-day model (walkforward.py --remaining --dump; every probability out of sample, each month's models fitted on the dates before it). Jeddah and Istanbul, the event day itself, decisions from 10:00 to before 17:00 on the city's clock, event dates up to DEV_LAST: the ledger's dates already looked at (data/eval/wxpredict/exposure_ledger.json, untouched_from 10 Oct). The dump's later rows are dropped before anything is scored, and the walk-forward's own log loss of its October month is not read. THE BOOKS: the archived books (data/archive/books, data/mirror/book_snapshots), a snapshot every hour 12-25 Sep and every two hours from 26 Sep. Each book is judged with the newest decision of its city-day at or before it, at most an hour old (as ask_backtest.py). The ladder at size is rebuilt from the archived depth tiers by the platform's rule (execution.synth_levels): the first tier is priced at the touch, which is optimistic, so every result is also shown with that tier one cent dearer. THE RULE: sdyes.walk_yes and sdyes.choose. YES only; a ticket of $10; a level is bought while p - (price + taker fee) >= THETA; at least 5 shares (the minimum order is not in the archived books); one entry per city-day, the first book at which a bucket qualifies, held to settlement on the venue's winner. WHO: the candidates p_weather (the remaining-day model alone) and p_fusion (it pooled with the market, the WXPredict incumbent); the controls q (the market's own prices: market-only) and p_tempered (the market recalibrated); and rd1 (S10, the live same-day incumbent), at its own checkpoints, where one is at most an hour before the book. THE CHOICE, fixed before the run: among the two candidates and THETA in THETAS, the pair with the highest mean net profit per entry date (Jeddah and Istanbul together) with at least MIN_ENTRY_DATES entry dates. If no pair has a positive mean, nothing is frozen: the pilot stops at development and that is reported.",
